  "worked_solution": "First, we find the limit of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to \\infty }f(t) & =\u27e8{lim}_{t\\to \\infty }{e}^{-t},\\,{lim}_{t\\to \\infty }{(1+\\frac{1}{t})}^{t},\\,{lim}_{t\\to \\infty }4\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e80,e,4\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that the second component of ${lim}_{t\\to \\infty }f(t)$ is a special limit.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to \\infty }g(t) & =\u27e8{lim}_{t\\to \\infty }\\frac{{t}^{2}}{1-{t}^{2}},\\,{lim}_{t\\to \\infty }\\frac{t+1}{t},\\,{lim}_{t\\to \\infty }{t}^{-5}\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8{lim}_{t\\to \\infty }\\frac{1}{(\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}-1)},\\,1+{lim}_{t\\to \\infty }\\frac{1}{t},\\,{lim}_{t\\to \\infty }\\frac{1}{{t}^{5}}\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8-1,1,0\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use properties of limits to calculate the final result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to \\infty }[f(t)\\cdot g(t)] & ={lim}_{t\\to \\infty }f(t)\\cdot {lim}_{t\\to \\infty }g(t) \\\\  & =\u27e80,\\,e,\\,4\u27e9\\cdot \u27e8-1,1,0\u27e9 \\\\  & =0\\cdot (-1)+e\\cdot 1+4\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =e\\end{aligned}\n$$",
